WEBVTT

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.150
A Sunrise Climb?

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.910
It's when you climb Mt. Fuji overnight 
to watch the sunrise from its peak.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.050
In the pitch dark,

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.850
you climb earnestly, as one of many points

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.010
forming a continuous line of lights.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.160
I was in high school then.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.540
It was also my first climb with my friend.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.130
As I had little sense of what 
to do, it was heart-pounding.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.340
Below was a sea of clouds,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.500
and a sky full of stars above.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.700
It was practically a whole different 
world from the one I'd always known.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.360
And then what?

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.110
My climber friend got exhausted halfway through.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.490
G-Go on ahead without me!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.610
Squeeze

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.240
Like in a drama, you know?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.650
He was physically strong,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.080
but apparently he'd paced himself wrong.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.040
So, I climbed to the top on my own,

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.770
and, along with many others on the 
summit, watched as the sky brightened.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.820
We were all gazing the same direction.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:47.500
That world, dyed bright red, 
was amazingly beautiful.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.220
It's a sight I'll never forget 
for the rest of my life.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.440
Mountain Trail

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.360
Season 2 - New Climb 6

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.690
Season 2 - New Climb 6
 In Order to Do What You Enjoy

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.240
S-Say, Hinata...

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.950
Well, I've been thinking on this, but...

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.500
Wh-Why don't <i>we</i> climb Mt. Fuji?!

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:15.860
Okay!

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.300
Mt. Fuji's a great idea!

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.810
I-I'll do my best.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:21.730
Yeah!

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.260
Even so...

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.870
What is it?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.890
Well, you'd disliked climbing 
so much until just recently.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.390
But now <i>you're</i> the one saying you want to go!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.400
Come on, don't tease me!

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.670
Okay, strike while the iron's hot!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.090
Let's go check out the equipment 
we'll need to climb Mt. Fuji!

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.030
We can't use the same equipment 
as for Mt. Mitsutouge?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.930
Since we'll be climbing at night, 
we'll need headlamps, right?

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.910
No street lamps up there!

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.920
Why not bring flashlights?

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.670
They only leave one hand free.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.290
Oh, true...

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.380
Also, since it gets cold even in summer,

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.920
they say you should dress for midwinter.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.170
Midwinter?!

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.930
Segment: Teach Us, Kaede-san!

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.700
Teach us, Kaede-san!

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:12.160
On mountains, the temperature drops 0.6 degrees 
Celsius with every 100 meters of increase in elevation.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.240
At an elevation of 3776 meters,

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:18.980
the temperature will be approximately 
22 degrees colder than at sea level.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.950
So if it's 30 C at the base of Mt. Fuji, 
it will be 8 C at the summit.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.940
Mt. Fuji has even had snowfall in August!

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.700
S-So that's why!

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.740
Since regular coats are heavy and bulky,

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.000
I recommend a light and 
warm down jacket instead.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.590
Outdoors
Camping
Mountain Climbing Supplies

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.040
Down jacket, huh...

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.090
Mt. Fuji
Visit Japan's 
Finest Mountain!

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.090
They've got a section for Mt. Fuji!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.280
Mt. Fuji really is a big deal!

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.680
Look, the necessities are listed here.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.350
Minimum Necessary 
Equipment

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:51.350
Work gloves?

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.350
Why would we need work gloves?

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.550
Beats me.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:59.360
On Mt. Fuji, there are places along 
the way where you climb over rocks.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.360
Work gloves are essential.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.610
Huh...

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.590
I-Is that so...

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.990
I'm pretty sure we have some at home.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.740
Head Lamp Pro Z

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.740
These are the headlamps!

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.740
Oh, like the ones they attach 
to construction helmets.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.510
There are a lot of them.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:16.750
Lumen?

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.180
I think that's brightness.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.620
A higher lumen value means it's brighter.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.840
I'll get this one!

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.020
Couldn't you just borrow your dad's?

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:29.800
Well...

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:36.810
Headlamps

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.660
I'm the one who dragged you 
into mountaineering, Aoi.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.810
It wouldn't be fair if I'm the only 
one who gets to borrow everything.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.280
Thank you.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.570
Next, a down jacket!

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.320
So many kinds!

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.810
This one's cute!

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.910
I really want it.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.990
Wait, that one's...

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.100
What?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.580
Ladies Trekking Down
Size: M    Color: 2

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.550
Thirty-nine thousand yen?!

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.050
This one's thirty thousand!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.470
This is <i>sixty</i> thousand?!

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.560
Down's got a high price...{not sure if she's making a pun on purpose, but it's possible}

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.180
I really can't afford these.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.180
Wh-What'll I do?

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:15.910
Maybe if I wear several sweaters,

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.980
along with a coat,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.230
Mountain Trail

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.170
I'll manage just fine?

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.320
Oh no!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.660
That reminds me, around New Year's, my mom...

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.890
Look at me, Aoi!

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.430
I bought a fashionable down jacket!

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.060
That's great!

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.460
Mom has one!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.630
I could borrow a down jacket from Mom!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.290
Wow, that's great!

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:47.710
In that case, couldn't I 
just borrow Dad's headlamp?

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.440
Didn't you already decide to buy one?

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.420
Go on, buy it!

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.930
All right, all right!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.180
I'm home!

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:57.860
Welcome home!

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.430
Say, Mom...

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.190
don't you have a down jacket?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.880
A down jacket?

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.690
Yes, but why?

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.980
I'd like to borrow it.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.550
But it's summertime.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.370
I thought I'd wear it when climbing Mt. Fuji.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.840
Mt. Fuji?!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.650
They say it gets cold even in summer.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.550
It's for "Sunrise Climbing,"

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:24.200
where people climb during the night 
to watch the sunrise from the summit.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.860
Mt. Fuji? At night?!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.390
Mountain climbing is dangerous enough already,

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.130
but climbing at night?!

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.420
Besides, you're a girl!

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.970
M-Mom?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:42.090
You've also been out late at night more often.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:43.730
Are you studying properly?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.830
Didn't your class rank fall 
at the end-of-term exams?

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:49.610
That had nothing to do with this...

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.900
I will never allow you to 
be on a mountain at night!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.120
Mt. Fuji 100%

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.050
Thanks for dinner...

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.360
What's the matter?

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.720
Mt. Fuji 100%

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:24.730
I see...

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.370
Aoi wants to visit Mt. Fuji.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.060
I'm worried that she might get into danger.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.520
She had no interest in things 
like mountains before.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:38.490
I'm sure she's found something she truly enjoys.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:41.490
I think that's good.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.500
I'm not so sure...

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.010
I'm coming in!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.780
Do you have a moment?

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:56.890
Yeah.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.260
Well, is climbing mountains fun for you?

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:04.960
Yeah.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.270
Last time, when I climbed 
Mt. Mitsutouge with my friends,

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.780
Mt. Fuji looked very pretty from there.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.780
And so, you plan to climb Mt. Fuji next?

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.300
That's not the only reason.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.120
I understand how your mother feels.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:29.460
It's natural to worry when your only daughter 
suddenly talks about climbing Mt. Fuji.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.220
But if you truly want to do it,

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:40.070
you need to explain yourself properly and 
persuade her that she has nothing to worry about.

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:47.280
Sorry to bother you. Good night.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.400
Mt. Fuji 100%

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.910
Mom, I still want to climb Mt. Fuji!

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.690
You're bringing this up again?

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.920
Mt. Fuji is a mountain even beginners can climb.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.860
While it's called a night climb,

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.030
they arrive at mountain huts near 
the summit while it's still light out,

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.830
so the nighttime part of the climb is 
only the two or three hours before dawn.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.120
Also, a senior from my school who knows 
mountains will come along with us,

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.560
and teach us everything 
we need to know in advance!

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:30.010
And cell phones get reception there, 
so I'll contact you regularly.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.230
So, please let me go, Mom!

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:44.290
<i>It seems she won't give up on this.</i>

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:47.960
All right.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.420
I'll allow it just this once.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:51.840
Really?!

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.170
But you'll need to keep 
that promise you just made.{i.e., to call regularly}

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:57.670
Okay!

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:01.970
Here.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.920
Your down jacket...

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.330
Are you sure?

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:07.970
Aoi...

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:12.130
I may worry about you,

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.980
but I'm not being critical.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:18.230
If there's anything you need from me, 
you can ask me any time, okay?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.520
Okay!

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.990
Thank you, Mom!

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:32.590
I'm still not sure this is for the best.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:37.000
However, this is the first time I've 
seen Aoi so intent to do something.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.510
She's grown strong.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.760
I have somewhat mixed feelings about that.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.760
<i>I think I understand a little better.</i>

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.540
<i>If you wish for something with all your heart,</i>

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.260
<i>you can find a way.</i>

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:52.630
<i>Mt. Fuji...</i>

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:55.520
<i>is still a long way away,</i>

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.720
<i>but I'll do my best!</i>

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued!
